Problem 1. Explain, in your own words, the differences and similarities of
interfaces, abstract classes, and classes.


Problem 2. Explain, in your own words, the concept of inheritance.


Problem 3. Answer the following questions:
• Can an interface inherit from an interface? from multiple interfaces?
from a class?
• Can a class inherit from an interface? from multiple interfaces?
• Can a class inherit from a class? from multiple classes?


Problem 4. Implement an object-oriented design of a vending machine,
considering the following requirements.
• A vending machine sells a number of products.
– A product has a name and a price.
– A product has a unique slot in the vending machine.
– There is a number of items for each product in the vending machine (e.g. we can have 5 units of the product “chocolate” in our
vending machine).
– A product may be stocked or sold out.
• We can have perishable and non-perishable products.
– Each perishable product has an expiration date.
