– Each non-perishable product has a “best-before” date.
• Some of the products are sold in plastic bottles (e.g. sodas) and should
specify the number of millilitres they contain.
– They should have this method:
int getNumberOfMillilitres().


Problem 5. Implement an object-oriented design of a smart fridge. This
exercise is intended to be open-ended. Use your imagination! Here are some
questions to get started:
• What items does a fridge contain?
• What categories can these items be grouped into?
• What kind of information is associated with these items?
• What operations can you perform on a fridge?
• What can go wrong and what can go right during fridge operation?
• What helpful features could you imagine from a “smart” fridge?
• A fridge is not just a fridge. What are some fancy features supported
by fridges?
Try to come up with a meaningful design. I expect several interfaces or
abstract-classes.
Hint: If you ever get stuck, just go to your fridge, and look inside.